{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115829","id":3242164149,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7BP3-1","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115829","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115829.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115829.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115829","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115829/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115829/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115829/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d0eb19359e27a14b4cd3a920fdc3cf1b81a89848","number":115829,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"GDScript: Fix compiler generates incorrect bytecode for conversion return","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR fixes a bug I noticed during review #115763:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc test(object: Object) -> Node:\r\n    return object\r\n\r\nfunc output(value: Variant) -> void:\r\n    if value is Object:\r\n        var object: Object = value\r\n        print(\"<%s>\" % object.get_class())\r\n    else:\r\n        print(var_to_str(value).replace(\"\\n\", \"\"))\r\n\r\nfunc _run() -> void:\r\n    # Before: Prints `<Resource>`.\r\n    # After: Runtime error `Trying to return a value of type \"Resource\" from\r\n    #                       a function whose return type is \"Node\".`.\r\n    output(test(Resource.new()))\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe reason was that type compatibility checking was performed in the code generator and had a bug (it generated `OPCODE_RETURN` instead of `OPCODE_RETURN_TYPED_NATIVE`).\r\n\r\nI removed the duplicate bytecode generation code (the first branch was missing checks for the `GDScriptDataType::{NATIVE,SCRIPT,GDSCRIPT}` cases) and moved the conversion check logic to the analyzer; the compiler passes the result to the code generator using the `use_conversion` field (similar to `use_conversion_assign` in `AssignableNode`, `AssignmentNode`, and `ForNode`). The code generator isn't actually designed for type checking because it deals with `GDScriptDataType` instead of `GDScriptParser::DataType`.\r\n\r\nTest script:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nclass A:\r\n    func f1() -> Node: return null\r\n    func f2(x: Object) -> Node: return x\r\n    func f3(x: Node2D) -> Node: return x\r\n    #func f4(x: Resource) -> Node: return x # Analyzer error.\r\n```\r\n\r\nBytecode (before):\r\n\r\n```\r\nFunction f1()\r\n 0: line 2:     func f1() -> Node: return null\r\n 2: return const(<null>)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction f2(x)\r\n 0: line 3:     func f2(x: Object) -> Node: return x\r\n 2: return stack(3)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction f3(x)\r\n 0: line 4:     func f3(x: Node2D) -> Node: return x\r\n 2: return stack(3)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n```\r\n\r\nBytecode (after):\r\n\r\n```\r\nFunction f1()\r\n 0: line 2:     func f1() -> Node: return null\r\n 2: return const(<null>)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction f2(x)\r\n 0: line 3:     func f2(x: Object) -> Node: return x\r\n 2: return typed native (const(class(Node))) stack(3)\r\n 5: == END ==\r\n\r\nFunction f3(x)\r\n 0: line 4:     func f3(x: Node2D) -> Node: return x\r\n 2: return stack(3)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI also made the VM error messages more consistent and complete (using the `_get_var_type()` function). Given that I didn't have to update other unit tests, it appears there were no tests at all for returning values ​​prior to #115763.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nFinally, this PR slightly optimizes the bytecode for return statements that return a typed array or dictionary of the same type as the function's return type. In this case, we can simply use `OPCODE_RETURN` instead of `OPCODE_RETURN_TYPED_ARRAY` or `OPCODE_RETURN_TYPED_DICTIONARY`, since type checking is not required at runtime.\r\n\r\nTest script:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc f(x: Array[int]) -> Array[int]:\r\n    return x\r\n```\r\n\r\nBytecode (before):\r\n\r\n```\r\nFunction f(x)\r\n 0: line 2:     func f(x: Array[int]) -> Array[int]: return x\r\n 2: return typed array stack(3)\r\n 7: == END ==\r\n```\r\n\r\nBytecode (after):\r\n\r\n```\r\nFunction f(x)\r\n 0: line 2:     func f(x: Array[int]) -> Array[int]: return x\r\n 2: return stack(3)\r\n 4: == END ==\r\n```","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"ht